description: Rules against fake or incomplete implementation
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Fake Completion

- Do not call a feature complete if it is only visually mocked when functionality is required.
- During frontend-only phases, mock data is allowed intentionally.
- During backend/dynamic phases, replace required mock data with real functionality.
- Do not leave fake buttons that imply unavailable functionality.
- Do not fabricate API responses, database records or success messages.
- Clearly distinguish mock/demo behavior from production functionality.
